// A regression for the difference observer: a program that prints the
// clock and a random number. The judge fixes the seed and the clock for
// both of its runs, so two runs that differ only in the planted secret
// print the same, and this holds. Without those fixed, randomness alone
// would score "broken". check_ctf.py judges it under a budget that grants
// clock and rand, which no claim's budget does.
fn main() uses io, clock, rand {
    print(format("now {} random {} {} {}", now(), random(1000000),
                 random(1000000), random(1000000)))
}
